y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101991/selection/15218410491760fde7a5ee3424ab85ac6b1f2282de29d6ccd23fa0e4a3383a11" :answer/id #uuid "343d1790-9290-574e-aea2-cddafbb5cf00" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-10,$ $x=-5,$  and $x=0$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101991/selection/09a24208711d41dc6b54c3eea297996391a410200970f3748660ed608eaeb209" :answer/id #uuid "71541ac7-8988-5aa5-9dcf-893226b0bdd1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-10$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101991/selection/3d9482eabd5d50942c08e64fff899b513485e524b397ba3c1855281c08d34888" :answer/id #uuid "b5f653f3-165c-5e22-b98b-66497534353a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-5$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101991/selection/315b43fa6f64ecaa42242af20d22500e5878dad9f38069ad69d3bbb24147f539" :answer/id #uuid "abea6dbd-cbc4-5e27-a20a-3c43e9c4070a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-10$ and $x=-5$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101991/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d1a74be8-16fd-5929-85ad-92fc12e791c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-101991/selection/315b43fa6f64ecaa42242af20d22500e5878dad9f38069ad69d3bbb24147f539" :answer-field/choices ["q-101991/selection/517b13fa7d7411493417798333c215e538be20515774e23158b4c71536604686" "q-101991/selection/15218410491760fde7a5ee3424ab85ac6b1f2282de29d6ccd23fa0e4a3383a11" "q-101991/selection/09a24208711d41dc6b54c3eea297996391a410200970f3748660ed608eaeb209" "q-101991/selection/3d9482eabd5d50942c08e64fff899b513485e524b397ba3c1855281c08d34888" "q-101991/selection/315b43fa6f64ecaa42242af20d22500e5878dad9f38069ad69d3bbb24147f539"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-101991" :question/id #uuid "8b49effd-34ee-539b-94bb-4a761d8bf290" :question/math-academy-id "q-101991" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981111/assets/6ec1bb6f164aa4878480f06707722769d1e17ff735a04c29a3fc2b9bd09ca467.png)\n\nConsider the function $y=f(x)$ whose graph is plotted above. At which points is the function $f(x)$ **not** differentiable?" :question/worked-solution "The function is not differentiable wherever it has a discontinuity, corner, cusp, or vertical tangent.\n\n- At $x=-10$ the function has a corner, so it's not differentiable there.\n\n- At $x=-5$ the function has an infinite discontinuity, so it's not differentiable there.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x=-10$ and $x=-5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-101991/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7dcbd56f-0fc2-59c5-a016-4272be4734c7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-101991"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-102163/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "2c24a4c5-5774-5e61-9500-ac29447b5de2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102163/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "4dc1c01b-0fec-517d-99c1-76388bbf37c1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102163/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "bda7d1bf-2be3-55d6-9338-f0cc39fd2b3a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102163/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "2b9df08e-5be5-561b-987c-e879133c9de7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102163/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "86b056ee-6fd7-5a9b-90d6-a4641b906f0f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102163/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6c5b356e-1847-5521-9d23-2557c1554c47" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-102163/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-102163/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-102163/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-102163/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-102163/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-102163/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-102163" :question/id #uuid "c7c7ee1b-da55-5996-923f-38ff8f88ec23" :question/math-academy-id "q-102163" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function given below?\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}2x-2, & x<0 \\\\ -2, & x\\ge 0\\end{aligned}\\,\n$$\n\n- It is continuous at $x=0$\n- It is differentiable at $x=0$\n- It is differentiable on the interval $(0,2)$" :question/worked-solution "- Statement I is true  Indeed, let's investigate the continuity of $f(x).$ It is continuous everywhere except, possibly, at  $x=0.$ At this point, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}(2x-2)=2(0)-2=-2 \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}-2=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}f(x)=f(0)=-2,\n$$\n\nand so $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=0$ .\n\n- Statement II is false, $f(x)$ is not differentiable at $x=0$ because it has a corner point there: \n\n$\\,$ ${f}^{′}(x)=2\\,$  if  $\\,x<0$ and ${f}^{′}(x)=0\\,$ if $\\,x>0$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, $f(x)$ is differentiable everywhere except at $x=0.$   Since $x=0$  doesn't belong to $(0,2)$, the given function is differentiable on this interval.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and III are true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-102163/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1b4100f8-8a66-5243-b0b6-c36b9d17dac3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-102163"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
